#: ../../source/guide/tools.md:1 2d40041004e4485786991d3fc303b95e
msgid "工具参考"
msgstr "Tool Reference"

#: ../../source/guide/tools.md:3 dae0543359ae454d85e178df0fb181f6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"中栏工具面板接通八个工具：轨道族生成、任务轨道设计、参数空间扫描 （catalog_sweep）、轨道保持、轨道预报、转移轨道设计、时空坐标转换与"
" 分区边界（spatiography_boundaries）；轨道稳定性因上游 placeholder （空参 "
"schema）暂不接入。参数面板由工具的 JSON Schema 自动生成：字段范围、 默认值与说明来自 e2m2e 的 Pydantic "
"模型；按 `orbit_type` 裁剪，只显示当前族 适用的字段；Optional 字段以勾选控制传不传值（勾选即传、不勾视为未设置）。 "
"本页展开说明轨道族生成与转移设计，其余工具的参数见各 schema 与 {doc}`../dev/architecture`。"
msgstr "The middle-column tool panel wires eight tools: orbit family generation, orbit design, parameter sweep (catalog_sweep), station keeping, orbit propagation, transfer design, spacetime transform, and spatiography boundaries (spatiography_boundaries); stability analysis stays out while upstream marks it a placeholder (empty-arg schema). Parameter forms are generated from each tool's JSON Schema: field ranges, defaults and descriptions come from e2m2e's Pydantic models; fields are pruned by `orbit_type` so only those applicable to the current family appear; Optional fields are controlled by checkboxes (checked sends the value, unchecked leaves it unset). This page covers family generation and transfer design in depth; for the rest, see each schema and {doc}`../dev/architecture`."

#: ../../source/guide/tools.md:12 bd3c04a02c474d729079b9a14e2664b2
msgid "轨道族生成（orbit_family_generation）"
msgstr "Orbit Family Generation (orbit_family_generation)"

#: ../../source/guide/tools.md:14 c0828c11003d447f95cb4b46de634bc9
msgid ""
"在 CR3BP 中生成轨道族：周期族（Halo / NRHO / Axial / SPO / LPO / Horseshoe） "
"为延拓，Lissajous 为拟周期轨迹的参数采样，DRO 为月心族（不绑定平动点）。 范围与默认值由 e2m2e "
"`FamilyGenerationRequest` 的 `valid_ranges` 决定，GUI 不另维护一份。纯 CR3BP 计算，不需要 "
"SPICE 内核。"
msgstr ""
"Generates orbit families in the CR3BP: periodic families (Halo / NRHO / "
"Axial / SPO / LPO / Horseshoe) by continuation, Lissajous by parameter "
"sampling of quasi-periodic bounded trajectories, DRO as a Moon-centred "
"family (not bound to a libration point). Ranges and defaults come from "
"the e2m2e `FamilyGenerationRequest` `valid_ranges`; the GUI keeps no copy"
" of its own. Pure CR3BP computation - no SPICE kernels needed."

